    "notes": "Original geometry from current Rappange restoration images and OSM/BAG outline. Groote Museum w269020374 is a separate building and remains untouched. Conservatory within existing parent; no plaza ground. Heights estimated from photographed storeys and proportions. Black box central hall addition, not a separate duplicate building. Current BAG reveals both 12m end pavilions absent from old OSM 53m central hall outline, giving total built frontage ~78m. Its rear 40m-wide projection is the built glazed conservatory visible in Rappange restoration photographs, not a courtyard. Roofed mass follows photographed pavilions, low hall, central dark box and glass conservatory separately."
